        "original_id": "3903455a-9e6c-5914-8629-8f5992e7067a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sidney Olcott, Denis Villeneuve, Gene Gauntier\n- Works: From the Manger to the Cross, Maelström, Polytechnique, Incendies, Enemy\n- Awards: Canadian Screen Award, Genie Award\n- Roles: film producer, director, actor, screenwriter, writer, actress\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Olcott was born on September 20, 1872, and died on December 16, 1949.\n- Sidney Olcott was a Canadian-born film producer, director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- Denis Villeneuve was born on October 3, 1967, and is a French Canadian film director and writer.\n- Denis Villeneuve won the Canadian Screen Award, formerly called the Genie Award, for Best Direction four times.\n- Denis Villeneuve won Best Direction for Maelström in 2001.\n- Denis Villeneuve won Best Direction for Polytechnique in 2010.\n- Denis Villeneuve won Best Direction for Incendies in 2011.\n- Denis Villeneuve won Best Direction for Enemy in 2013.\n- Sidney Olcott directed From the Manger to the Cross and also appeared in the film.\n- Gene Gauntier wrote the script for From the Manger to the Cross and portrayed the Virgin Mary.",
